# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Reference corpus — NEVER commit.
#
# Archived third-party catalog pages are analysis input only. Statistical
# properties derived from them (distributions, co-occurrence, naming grammar)
# are facts about how the industry models this data and DO ship. The captured
# pages themselves are someone else's compilation and do NOT.
#
# If you find yourself wanting to commit something under one of these paths,
# the answer is to derive a statistic from it and commit that instead.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
raw/
corpus/
reference/
*.warc
*.warc.gz
captures/

# Rendered output can be large and is reproducible from the generator.
out/
dist/

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.v/
.DS_Store
.agent/

# Build output (gen#536): scripts/build_derived.py writes these, CI uploads them as an artifact.
build/
golden-retail/stats.json
docs/figures.md
docs/retail-apparel-decoys.md
prototypes/retail_drawings/samples*.ndjson
prototypes/retail_drawings/preview*.html
